# PROJECT
SEO-first INFORMATIONAL IPTV blog (UK en-GB, US en-US). No sales, no product pages.
Stack: Astro 4+, TypeScript strict, Tailwind, MDX. Static generation only.

# NON-NEGOTIABLES
- All indexable content is statically rendered. No client-side rendering for content.
- Copy and articles live in /content (MDX/JSON), never hardcoded in components.
- Never link to playlists, resellers or unlicensed services.
- Never invent stats, reviews, prices, quotes or channel counts. Use TODO placeholders.
- No AggregateRating/Review schema without real reviews.

# SEO RULES (every page)
- Unique title (<=60 chars, keyword first), description (<=155), canonical, OG, Twitter.
- One H1, logical H2/H3, breadcrumbs, TOC, published + updated dates, author box.
- JSON-LD via /lib/seo.ts only: Article, FAQPage, HowTo, BreadcrumbList, Person.
- 3+ contextual internal links per article, descriptive anchors, max 3 clicks from home.
- Images: AVIF/WebP, width/height, alt text, lazy except LCP. Fonts: self-hosted, swap.

# PERFORMANCE
LCP < 2.0s, CLS < 0.05, INP < 200ms, < 100KB JS per page. Reserved ad slots, no layout shift.

# WORKFLOW
- Small steps. After each change run lint, typecheck and `npm run seo-check`.
- Explain decisions briefly and list files changed.
- Articles under 800 words (pillars under 1800) must fail seo-check.